WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.002 --> 00:00:02.460
JENNY BROWN: Hiring great people
is core to every business,

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.070
but finding the right talent
is often the tricky part.

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.690
Traditional job
sites aim to help

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.270
people find jobs
and jobs find people

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:12.100
but can have difficulty
returning relevant results.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.520
Let's dive into how you can
use Google's Cloud Talent

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.500
Solution to leverage
machine learning

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.630
and create a better
job search experience.

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:22.018
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:25.960
See, large companies may have
their own internal hiring

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.420
and recruiting teams, whereas,
smaller companies might

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.370
use off-the-shelf
talent solutions,

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:33.280
but both want quality results
for candidates and job

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.480
postings.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.580
Trying to match these
together may sound simple

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.070
on the surface, but traditional
keyword searching is

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:41.260
too simplistic and
gets choked up in some

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:45.130
situations, such as hidden or
extraneous keywords, also known

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:47.260
as keyword stuffing;
job postings

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.210
that require five
years of experience

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:52.120
in a technology that's really
only been around for two years;

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:54.840
and things like typos,
acronyms, and overuse

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.240
of technical jargon.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.860
What exactly is a [? rec ?] and
asset prot [? 1? ?] Ultimately,

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:02.860
these lead to poor experiences
and bad candidate fits.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:05.050
So Google used
machine learning, also

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:07.750
called ML, to create a
customizable job searching

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:09.160
experience.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.960
The Cloud Talent
Solution job search

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.150
API is designed to
power the job search

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:16.120
experience with built-in
machine learning algorithms.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.250
In short, you send your
job listing information

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:20.440
over, such as the
company and job details,

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.180
to the job search API.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.460
The API analyzes the
job data to develop

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:26.470
an understanding of the jobs.

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:28.540
Once jobs have been
indexed by the API,

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.790
you can search against the
jobs and get search results

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.340
by relevance or other
sorting preferences,

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:35.290
which we'll talk about
in future videos.

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.360
There are four common
use cases that typically

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.010
leverage a solution like this--

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.900
job boards where the
site returns a list

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.900
of jobs to job seekers,
career site providers that

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.840
provide career site services
to client companies,

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.990
staffing agencies which provide
short or long-term employees

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:52.660
to clients, and applicant
tracking systems which

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:55.180
are used by companies to track
applicants through the hiring

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:56.000
process.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.900
The job search API is designed
to be modified to best fit

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:00.970
with your needs, and
the API's performance

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:03.940
can vary significantly based
on how it's configured.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:07.300
Also, it's worth noting that
the job search API is not

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.370
to be confused with
the jobs indexing

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:11.650
API that facilitates
jobs showing up

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.240
on google.com Search.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:16.000
There's a separate indexing API
to have job listings show up

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.078
on searches that people
make on google.com.

00:02:18.078 --> 00:02:19.870
There's a link for this
in the description,

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.590
if you want to learn
more about that,

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.770
but the Cloud Talent
Solution job search API

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:26.440
does much more when it's
integrated into your job search

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:27.310
solution.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:28.930
With all that being
said, let's talk

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:31.690
about how to actually
implement the job search API.

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:33.580
In our next video,
we'll go over the API

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:35.530
in greater detail,
planning steps,

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:38.050
and talk more about
implementation strategies.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.730
Thanks for watching,
and remember,

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:43.290
when looking for talent, it's OK
to keep your head in the cloud.

